From: Geoffrey Thomas <kztbbv97dh@privaterelay.appleid.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Jun 2026
Subject: [PATCH] sleep: fall back to boot-time check when timerfd POLLIN races

On AMD platforms the RTC alarm that backs CLOCK_BOOTTIME_ALARM routes
through the EC.  When the alarm fires the EC raises GPE 0x0B (ACPI SCI,
IRQ 9), which wakes s2idle and sets pm_wakeup_irq=9.  The timerfd's own
POLLIN callback fires through a separate in-kernel path, but it can
arrive a few milliseconds after the EC path has already caused s2idle to
exit and user-space to resume.  By the time fd_wait_for_event(tfd,
POLLIN, 0) is called with a zero timeout the timerfd is not yet readable,
so the code treats the wake as a manual wakeup and skips hibernate.

The race exists in two code paths:

1. custom_timer_suspend(): woken_by_timer = FLAGS_SET(r, POLLIN) — if
   false, the function returns 0 (no hibernate) even when the deadline
   has passed.

2. execute_s2h() hardware-BTP path: if (FLAGS_SET(r, POLLIN)) — if
   false, falls through to return 0 (no hibernate).

Fix both by adding a CLOCK_BOOTTIME fallback.

In custom_timer_suspend(), hibernate_timestamp is computed at function
entry (line 405) but the timerfd interval is measured from a later
before_timestamp (line 447), so the timer fires 1–2 seconds before
hibernate_timestamp.  Resume latency from s2idle is sub-second, so a
plain >= check would be false.  Use a 5-second grace period to cover
this structural gap while remaining safe against legitimate manual
wakeups (which occur seconds to minutes early, not within 5 s of the
deadline).

In execute_s2h() the timerfd is reprogrammed each cycle from the
current time so the gap is negligible; a plain >= check suffices.

---
 src/sleep/sleep.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/sleep/sleep.c b/src/sleep/sleep.c
--- a/src/sleep/sleep.c
+++ b/src/sleep/sleep.c
@@ -500,7 +500,7 @@
                 if (r < 0)
                         return log_error_errno(r, "Error polling timerfd: %m");
                 /* Store fd_wait status */
-                woken_by_timer = FLAGS_SET(r, POLLIN);
+                woken_by_timer = FLAGS_SET(r, POLLIN) || now(CLOCK_BOOTTIME) + 5 * USEC_PER_SEC >= hibernate_timestamp;

                 r = fetch_batteries_capacity_by_name(&current_capacity);
                 if (r < 0 || hashmap_isempty(current_capacity)) {
@@ -577,7 +577,7 @@
                                 r = fd_wait_for_event(tfd, POLLIN, 0);
                                 if (r < 0)
                                         return log_error_errno(r, "Error polling timerfd: %m");
-                                if (FLAGS_SET(r, POLLIN)) {
+                                if (FLAGS_SET(r, POLLIN) || now(CLOCK_BOOTTIME) >= hibernate_timestamp) {
                                         /* Timer fired - but respect HibernateOnACPower setting */
                                         if (!sleep_config->hibernate_on_ac_power && on_ac_power() > 0) {
